The [[Fuchsia Gym]] specializes in {{type|Poison}} Pokémon. Poison-type moves are super effective against {{type|Grass}} Pokémon, while Poison-type Pokémon are weak to {{t|Ground}}- and {{type|Psychic}} moves.

The Gym Leader is trained in the skills of the ninja, and has installed a series of nearly invisible glass panels to disorient any challengers. In addition, each of the Gym Trainers has disguised themselves as the [[Gym Leader]]. Follow the east wall toward the back of the building, then loop around toward the front. The Gym Leader is located near the center of the building.

[[Janine]]'s Pokémon use {{status|poisoning}} and {{status|confusion}} to incapacitate their opponent. Her {{p|Crobat}} is fast, so hit it with {{t|Psychic}}-, {{t|Electric}}-, {{t|Ice}}-, or {{type|Rock}} attacks to take it down quickly. Her {{p|Weezing}} is dangerous, as {{m|Toxic}} badly poisons the target, and {{m|Explosion}} is a last-ditch move that deals massive damage. Its phsycial {{stat|Defense}} is high, so use Psychic-type moves to target its lower {{stat|Special Defense}} instead. Her two {{p|Ariados}} can confuse the target with {{m|Swagger}} and lower the target's Speed with {{m|Scary Face}}. Her {{p|Venomoth}} prefers to use poison- and confusion-inducing moves. As {{t|Bug}} Pokémon, both it and her two Ariados take serious damage from {{t|Fire}}-, Rock-, and {{type|Flying}} attacks.

